WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.772
There are many vector-search tools, and students do not need to memorize every product.

00:00:06.772 --> 00:00:11.812
Instead, focus on the categories and the engineering tradeoffs.

00:00:11.812 --> 00:00:17.607
FAISS is a fast local vector-search library, but it is not a full database.

00:00:17.607 --> 00:00:21.502
Chroma is convenient for local prototypes.

00:00:21.502 --> 00:00:26.632
Qdrant is a vector database with strong metadata filtering.

00:00:26.632 --> 00:00:34.825
pgvector keeps vector search inside PostgreSQL, which can be attractive for teams already using relational data.

00:00:35.358 --> 00:00:37.950
Pinecone is a managed cloud service.

00:00:37.950 --> 00:00:43.045
Weaviate supports vector and hybrid search with a broader platform around it.

00:00:43.045 --> 00:00:47.980
Milvus and Zilliz are designed for larger-scale vector workloads.

00:00:47.980 --> 00:00:56.845
The syntax changes from product to product, but the pattern stays familiar: create or connect to a collection or index,

00:00:56.845 --> 00:01:05.390
insert vectors with metadata, embed the query, search for nearby vectors, and return the associated text.

00:01:05.390 --> 00:01:09.115
Choose based on the project, not on popularity.
